  "notes": "ADR-037 RBAC Runtime Wire completed. Changes:\n\n1. Fixed checkWorkerAuthority() bug — was always returning true even on violation, now returns false on scope violation\n2. Added console.error AUTHORITY_VIOLATION stdout message on violation\n3. Added emitAuthorityViolation event stream emit on violation\n4. Added guardedFileWrite() — RBAC-checked file write that throws ScopeViolationError + writes NO_GO result on violation\n5. Added validateTaskScope() for task execution start validation\n6. 9 tests covering: in-scope write, out-of-scope filesWrite, out-of-scope directories, event stream AUTHORITY_VIOLATION, guardedFileWrite throw, NO_GO result write, self-modifying sprint bypass\n\nNote: authority-enforcer.ts already had correct exports — no changes needed there. The core issue was (a) checkWorkerAuthority returning true on violations and (b) not being called anywhere. The function is now correct and guardedFileWrite provides the call-site integration pattern.",
